Per-file license breakdown for `open-assets/tween/`:

| File | License | Origin |
| ---- | ------- | ------ |
| `INTEGRATION.md` | MIT (this repo) | Hand-authored by hackathon-prep maintainers |
| `LitMotion/LICENSE` | MIT (Yusuke Nakada / Annulus Games) | Verbatim from https://github.com/annulusgames/LitMotion/blob/master/LICENSE |
| `LitMotion/README.md`, `LitMotion/README_JA.md` | MIT (Yusuke Nakada / Annulus Games) | Reference only |
| `LitMotion/src/LitMotion/Assets/LitMotion/**` | MIT (Yusuke Nakada / Annulus Games) | Reference — install via UPM, not by copying into your Unity project |
| `LitMotion/samples/LitMotion.Samples/**` | MIT (Yusuke Nakada / Annulus Games) | Reference — official LitMotion.Samples Unity project (do NOT copy into your project; sample-only) |

**Install via UPM, do NOT clone into your project**:

```json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "com.annulusgames.lit-motion": "https://github.com/annulusgames/LitMotion.git?path=/src/LitMotion/Assets/LitMotion#2.0.2"
  }
}
```

Official source: https://github.com/annulusgames/LitMotion (tag v2.0.2). The
shallow clone kept in this prep pack has had its `.git/` directory removed
(2026-10-15 fix Y6); the rest of the upstream source tree is kept as
reference material for grep/inspection without network.